ith this beer)</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>•</span></span></span><strong><span><span><span> Ardent Winter Ale</span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/5218ceb2-b628-d6a2-72f0-5b189fc0af28.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>❄️ 4X Southern Tier<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> 2XMAS</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Spiced Double Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Old Man Winter</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Ale<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Black Forest Cake</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Imperial Stout<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Fireside Cocoa</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Porter</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/cfe5ac92-35e3-d199-363b-b0d0556ae070.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🥳 Party packs<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Great Lakes Holiday Pack</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> with Christmas Ale, Cran Orange Wheat, Cookie Exchange Milk Stout, and the new Snowscape Winter Lager<br>•</span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span> Dogfish Head Pass the Aux Variety Pack</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> with Favorite Sweater IPA, Indian Brown Ale, Punkin Ale and Namaste White Ale</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/7296ffbf-0df2-ea69-e1d9-7e8f9dc5b2d1.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🙃 Happy Halloween<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Victory Merry Monkey</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Belgian Ale with cranberry, orange peel, cinnamon &amp; nutmeg<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Port City Tidings</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Belgian Blonde with coriander, cardamom, fresh ginger &amp; Grains of Paradise<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Straffe Hendrik Xmas Blend</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Quad<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>New Belgium Winter Quad</span></span></span></span></strong></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d985a0a2-5357-996a-01e6-ce86b4ab627d.png\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span>🏰 &nbsp;Incoming local fav!</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Silver Branch Obsidian Castle </span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>Tmavé Special Czech </span></span></span></span><span><span><span>Dark Lager</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>*expected Friday*</span></span></span></p>\n<p>Prison City Mass Riot Hazy IPA</p>\n<p>Full Distance Teufelsdrachen Dunkel</p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/4547f2b9-c9ad-1a70-ad16-42e768e924d2.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Philippe Guerin Abstraction #1 Muscadet Serve et Maine Sur Lie</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>Coming from a family winery that has been in continuous operation for five generations, this bottle is the perfect introduction (or friendly reminder) to Muscadet Sèvre et Maine Sur Lie. A crisp, mineral-driven wine with green apple, citrus zest, and a hint of sea breeze all of which perfectly cuts the creamy texture from the sur lie aging.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Le Meniere Sancerre</span></span><span><span>:</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span>An absolute classic of a Sancerre with notes of gooseberry, white peach and a bit of grassiness. Flinty and steely, this is a wine that is both delicate and sophisticated as well as powerful and savory.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Alias Merlot</span><span>: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Alias is a wine with a built-in secret identity, which is a nice twist for a grape that took a beating in the movie </span></span></span></span><em><span><span><span><span>Sideways. </span></span></span></span></em><span><span><span><span>Fortunately, Miles was wrong about Merlot as you'll see when you sip Alias Merlot. The perfect Tuesday night wine with raspberry and mulberry paired with violet, cedar and smoke.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong>La Griveliere Cotes du Rhone: </strong><span><span><span><span>We love Rhone reds around here, and La Griveliere delivers. Medium-bodied with great spice, nuanced fruit of black and red berries, pillowy tannins and that quintessential French grit.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span>Bonpas Châteauneuf-du-Pape Bonus Passus</span><span>: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>We have a thing for Chateauneuf-du-Pape (CDP). We love the big boldness paired with rustic French vibes. Jean-Luc Durand is a Grenache guy with a belief that Grenache gets better with age as the vines balance load naturally over time. Made with vines that average 65 years in age, Bonpas is warm and rich with plum, prune, tobacco and sweet spice all complemented by a silky smooth texture.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/4638d62e-cd03-5aab-cfb7-195a201acc93.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><span><span><span>As fall has finally found its way to the DMV, </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Ravines Cellars Dry Riesling</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> is a perfect fit for these cooler nights. With tasting notes of crisp pears and juicy white peaches finished off with a touch of minerality, this wine is an excellent way to help welcome in the pleasantly brisk fall evenings. This wine comes to us from the hillside overlooking the glacier-curved Seneca lake in the Finger Lakes wine region. The limestone and shale stone soil on the steep slopes where the grapes are grown provide a true dry Riesling taste with zippy clean notes. So, as you settle in for the night, pick up a bottle of this lovely Riesling to pair with your favorite fall dish.</span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Ben &amp; Sam B</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/d9fbdb97-b413-ec30-bc34-336ee4155d1b.png\" width=\"612\" alt=\"breathe11x17in_1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
